      "agent": "list, and a failed `SBMJOB` still falls through to the success message. I’ll pin the job name, job description, and library list, and turn a submit failure into an escape.\u001b[2m  auto-approved: write NIGHTLY.clle\u001b[0m\n\u001b[1m\n  NIGHTLY.clle\u001b[0m\n\u001b[31m  - /* Submit the nightly close. */\u001b[0m\n\u001b[31m  -              SBMJOB     CMD(CALL PGM(NIGHTCLS))\u001b[0m\n\u001b[32m  +              DCL        VAR(&MSGID) TYPE(*CHAR) LEN(7)\u001b[0m\n\u001b[32m  +              DCL        VAR(&FAILTXT) TYPE(*CHAR) LEN(80)\u001b[0m\n\u001b[32m  + \u001b[0m\n\u001b[32m  + /* Submit the nightly close under a fixed job name, job      */\u001b[0m\n\u001b[32m  + /* description and library list — not the caller's.          */\u001b[0m\n\u001b[32m  +              SBMJOB     CMD(CALL PGM(NIGHTCLS)) +\u001b[0m\n\u001b[32m  +                           JOB(NIGHTCLS) +\u001b[0m\n\u001b[32m  +                           JOBD(NIGHTLIB/NIGHTLY) +\u001b[0m\n\u001b[32m  +                           INLLIBL(NIGHTLIB QGPL QTEMP)\u001b[0m\n\u001b[32m  +              MONMSG     MSGID(CPF0000) EXEC(DO)\u001b[0m\n\u001b[32m  +                RCVMSG     MSGTYPE(*EXCP) MSGID(&MSGID) RMV(*NO)\u001b[0m\n\u001b[32m  +                CHGVAR     VAR(&FAILTXT) +\u001b[0m\n\u001b[32m  +                             VALUE('Nightly submit failed: ' *CAT +\u001b[0m\n\u001b[32m  +                             &MSGID)\u001b[0m\n\u001b[32m  +                SNDPGMMSG  MSGID(CPF9898) MSGF(QCPFMSG) +\u001b[0m\n\u001b[32m  +                             MSGDTA(&FAILTXT) MSGTYPE(*ESCAPE)\u001b[0m\n\u001b[32m  +              ENDDO\u001b[0m\n\n\u001b[2m  wrote NIGHTLY.clle\u001b[0m\n`NIGHTLY.clle` no longer submits with a bare `SBMJOB`. The nightly close is now submitted as job `NIGHTCLS`, under job description `NIGHTLIB/NIGHTLY`, with an initial library list of `NIGHTLIB`, `QGPL`, and `QTEMP`, so it no longer inherits the caller’s job description, library list, or output queue.\n\nThe submission itself is monitored. Any exception (`CPF0000`) is received, and the program sends `CPF9898` as an escape — `Nightly submit failed: ` plus the failing message id — instead of falling through to `Nightly submitted`.\n\u001b[2m  7595+7360 tokens · $0.0526\u001b[0m\n"
