      "agent": "emote, redaction strict\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\n\u001b[2m/help for the commands, Ctrl+C to quit.\n\u001b[0m\nI'll look up the transfer program and see how the two account updates are written today.\u001b[2m  0 match(es)\u001b[0m\n\u001b[2m  1 file(s)\u001b[0m\n\u001b[2m  read TRANSFER.sqlrpgle\u001b[0m\nThe two updates run independently, so a failure after the debit never credits the other account. I'll put them in one transaction and only commit when both SQLCODEs are zero.\u001b[2m  auto-approved: edit TRANSFER.sqlrpgle\u001b[0m\n\u001b[1m\n  TRANSFER.sqlrpgle\u001b[0m\n\u001b[31m  - exec sql\u001b[0m\n\u001b[31m  -   update ACCOUNT set BALANCE = BALANCE - :cents where ACCTNO = :fromAcct;\u001b[0m\n\u001b[31m  - \u001b[0m\n\u001b[31m  - exec sql\u001b[0m\n\u001b[31m  -   update ACCOUNT set BALANCE = BALANCE + :cents where ACCTNO = :toAcct;\u001b[0m\n\u001b[32m  + exec sql set option commit = *chg;\u001b[0m\n\u001b[32m  + \u001b[0m\n\u001b[32m  + exec sql\u001b[0m\n\u001b[32m  +   update ACCOUNT set BALANCE = BALANCE - :cents where ACCTNO = :fromAcct;\u001b[0m\n\u001b[32m  + \u001b[0m\n\u001b[32m  + if sqlcode <> 0;\u001b[0m\n\u001b[32m  +   inError = *on;\u001b[0m\n\u001b[32m  + else;\u001b[0m\n\u001b[32m  +   exec sql\u001b[0m\n\u001b[32m  +     update ACCOUNT set BALANCE = BALANCE + :cents where ACCTNO = :toAcct;\u001b[0m\n\u001b[32m  + \u001b[0m\n\u001b[32m  +   if sqlcode <> 0;\u001b[0m\n\u001b[32m  +     inError = *on;\u001b[0m\n\u001b[32m  +   endif;\u001b[0m\n\u001b[32m  + endif;\u001b[0m\n\u001b[32m  + \u001b[0m\n\u001b[32m  + if inError;\u001b[0m\n\u001b[32m  +   exec sql rollback;\u001b[0m\n\u001b[32m  + else;\u001b[0m\n\u001b[32m  +   exec sql commit;\u001b[0m\n\u001b[32m  +   if sqlcode <> 0;\u001b[0m\n\u001b[32m  +     inError = *on;\u001b[0m\n\u001b[32m  +     exec sql rollback;\u001b[0m\n\u001b[32m  +   endif;\u001b[0m\n\u001b[32m  + endif;\u001b[0m\n\n\u001b[2m  edited TRANSFER.sqlrpgle\u001b[0m\nBoth updates now share one commitment-control unit of work.\n\n- `SET OPTION COMMIT = *CHG` turns commitment control on for the module.\n- `SQLCODE` is checked after the debit, the credit, and the commit.\n- Both succeed and the commit returns zero: the transfer is committed and `inError` stays off.\n- Either update fails, or the commit itself fails: `inError` is set and the work is rolled back, so the debit cannot stand without the credit.\n\u001b[2m  10068+1473 tokens · $0.0188\u001b[0m\n"
